      "parsed_output": {
        "evidence": "Unpatched run output: \"[pov] VULNERABLE: file written outside outputDir at /tmp/zipslip-pov9011880755346885134/escaped.txt\" with EXIT=0. The vulnerable sink is ZipUtil.java Unpacker.process: line 1152 `File file = new File(outputDir, name);` followed by FileUtils.forceMkdir(file.getParentFile()) and FileUtils.copy(in, file) at lines 1157/1163, where `name` derives from the attacker-controlled zip entry name (mapper.map(zipEntry.getName())) with no restriction to outputDir. The same unvalidated join exists in Unwraper.process (line 1260) and BackslashUnpacker (line 1214).",
        "expected_vulnerable_behavior": "ZipUtil.unpack() extracts an entry named \"../escaped.txt\" and writes it to the parent of the requested output directory (path traversal), so the file at <base>/escaped.txt is created even though only <base>/out was the intended extraction root. The POV detects this out-of-bounds write and exits 0.",
        "notes": "The POV compiles ZipSlipPoV.java against the project's own target/classes plus its Maven runtime dependencies (resolved via mvn dependency:build-classpath for slf4j/commons), then runs it. It builds target/classes automatically if missing. It exercises the public ZipUtil.unpack(File, File) entry point (Unpacker branch) which is representative of all three vulnerable extraction branches (Unpacker/Unwraper/BackslashUnpacker) flagged in the alert. Runs inside /workspace/repo in the project container; no product code or normal tests were modified.",
